# Workflow gates

- Read [prd/README.md](prd/README.md) before product work.
- **No product features** until it names an **active phase** and the relevant `prd/` doc exists.
- **No invented requirements** — repo skills + `prd/` only (not Superpowers `brainstorming`; do not call ChatPRD MCP unless the **user** asks).
- **No application code** until `implement-from-prd` is run and the **user** approves the plan.
- **Scope:** implement only the active Linear issue / PRD section unless the **user** expands it.
- **Linear issues:** link `prd/…` + acceptance criteria; do not paste the full PRD.
- Before **user** review or authorized autonomous merge, run **`sql-gym-pre-review`** — it orchestrates an independent reviewer (no commits) and fixer; the implementer must not self-approve. Procedure: [.cursor/skills/sql-gym-pre-review/SKILL.md](.cursor/skills/sql-gym-pre-review/SKILL.md); checkboxes: [.github/pull_request_template.md](.github/pull_request_template.md) Agent pre-review section.
- Do **not** check PR boxes, ask for **user** review, or merge while blocking reviewer findings remain.
- Escalate to the **user** for product/architecture decisions or if stuck—do not mark boxes done to bypass a failed check.
- Do **not** merge PRs unless the **user** explicitly authorized autonomous merge for that run and PR type. When authorized, use GitHub MCP merge tools, not `gh` write commands.

# Agent references

- Phase, stack, dev commands: [prd/README.md](prd/README.md), [README.md](README.md), `./scripts/validate-env.sh`
- **Linear MCP** for backlog (`TIM-` issues, [sql-gym project](https://linear.app/times-api/project/sql-gym-ce6a8985c99e)). If lookup fails, ask the **user** to fix MCP auth in Cursor settings.
- **GitHub MCP** for PRs, comments, and authorized merges. Do not use `gh` write commands on cloud agents.
- **No committed secrets.** When the app exists, document vars in `.env.example`. On Cloud VMs, ask the **user** to add secrets in Cloud settings—do not assume a local `.env`.
- Playbook (plugins, Linear templates, examples): [docs/WORKFLOW.md](docs/WORKFLOW.md). Code style: [engineering.mdc](engineering.mdc).
